From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: separate O82 host clock timing from PHY cells

The active working Uke OEM capture has CLKOUT_TIMING zero on both
controllers. MiCode display 44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a
parses separate qcom,mdss-dsi-t-clk-pre/post properties; they are absent
from the selected O82 DT 4a3e1c391130237c5e8c2b250d1c94f3e25b9b11
and remain zero. PHY timing cells 12/13 are independently 20/0f.

After the admitted exact O82 PHY has written all fourteen correct cells,
export zero pre/post values to the host. The existing early timing helper
already refuses wrong machine, controller, D-PHY mode or clock window.
Other compatibles, PLL, divider, EOT, video timings and strength are unchanged.
Retain the measured panel, master-timing and post-link retime baseline; this
isolated change only corrects the exported host counters. Optical validation
remains required. Original GPL-2.0-only source attribution is retained.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1265,8 +1265,15 @@
 		writel(timing->shared_timings.clk_post,
 		       base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_TIMING_CTRL_13);
 	}
 
+	/* OEM host pre/post are separate from the fourteen PHY timing cells. */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(phy->pdev->dev.of_node,
+				    "xiaomi,uke-o82-dsi-phy-4nm")) {
+		timing->shared_timings.clk_pre = 0;
+		timing->shared_timings.clk_post = 0;
+	}
+
 	/* DSI lane settings */
 	dsi_phy_hw_v4_0_lane_settings(phy);
 
 	DBG("DSI%d PHY enabled", phy->id);
